# NOITE's street escape (3fstreet) starts the real XILINDRO, which wins:
# NOITE gets 0x40c (hides), then 0x40a, shows itself, adds the score and
# goes to the 3fstree2 cutscene, then back to the prison (3fprisao): the
# prison-escape SERIAL (minigameWon[2]) is not won here
# (xilindro-serial-hall.input wins both).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 93000 --input tools/play/xilindro-3fstreet-win.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --headless --scene 3fstreet --ms 96000 --fix all --input tools/play/xilindro-3fstreet-win.input
#
# The street video ends at 24795 (the WinExec); XILINDRO starts 1500 ms
# later (26295) and beats at once (alone, its first beat is 200 ms in), so
# the keys are xilindro-alone-win.input's, 26095 ms later:
# The keys follow one rule (planned against the port, beat by beat): the
# opponent walks in 32 px a beat and attacks on the beat after it comes
# within 130 px; in that 200-ms window the fighter steps Right (a 20-ms
# hold, released before the blow, so X4 never cuts it) when the opponent
# is beyond its 100-px reach, then kicks (Up, 2 points). The kick lands
# first and the opponent reels instead of attacking. Left steps back to
# x 0 while the opponent is far, so the fighter is never past x 50 when it
# kicks: no recoil (X11 never matters) and Right never meets the stand-off
# clamp (X10). The opponent never attacks, so `rand()` is never drawn (X3)
# and the Original and the Corrigida play the same fight: a KO with the
# fighter untouched, 91 x 150 = 13650 points.
# KO at 81895, XILINDRO closes at 86445.
20000 dump street
# The Corrigida (`--fix all`) shows XILINDRO's controls screen first; Enter takes
# it down 50 ms after it opened, PORRADA stands for 2 s (the frozen intro,
# `fight_controls.start_delay_ms`) and the round then plays as the
# Original's from its start, 2050 ms later (`delay`: every later line
# moves too).
# Its keys are the new layout: S is the middle kick (the Original's Up).
